ing has so far been minimal.\n\nThe national midterm environment favors Democrats, and the only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from July, showed Hurd ahead by just one point. Still, ten expert ratings split among Likely Republican, Lean Republican, and Tossup with a consensus of Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Romero roughly a one-in-four chance. September and October debates kept the race visible, but Hurd's incumbency, funding, and the district's lean make him the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -3.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2864, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.288, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3508, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2424, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2636, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3101, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3157, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3103, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3134, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3018, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3083, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3049, "margin": -3.5}]}